   25-27, 2008},
Organization = {Int Soc Mind, Brain \& Educ; SE Univ, Key Lab Child Dev \& Learning Sci;
   Thinktank - Handsbrain Educ; SE Univ State Key Lab Bioelect; Chinese Soc
   Biomed Elect},
Abstract = {In the educational field, affective factors are always ignored.
   Neuroscience researches. indicate that the brain areas involving
   cognition and emotions like the amygdale, the insula, the nucleus
   accumbens, the anterior cingulated cortex, the prefrontal cortex and so
   on highly overlap. Although Neuroscience seem not to directly relate
   with educational practice until now, the new-built knowledge about the
   emotional brain can help educators have an insight into the relationship
   between emotions and cognition. Affective education aims to improve
   students' affective abilities and make full use of the motivational,
   informative, communicative, regulative, and protective function of
   emotions to optimize students' learning. In the practice of affective
   education, the first must eradicate threats, and then teachers should
   involve emotions into teaching and learning by the following ways: (a)
   to model emotion exhibition about the learning and the subject; (b) to
   effectively process teaching material; (c) to make affective
   instruction.},
