Abstract = {Chemical pollution and carbon emissions are significant contributors to
   climate change. Accurately determining these emissions is challenging
   due to the lack of specialized analysis models. However, real-time
   emissions monitoring systems and the use of electric vehicles can bridge
   these gaps. Promoting public transportation and non-polluting modes of
   transportation can also contribute to reducing carbon emissions.
   Research in urban traffic areas has developed a method for evaluating
   chemical pollution using carbon footprints, which can provide practical
   solutions for reducing pollutant emissions and improving air quality. By
   adopting sustainable transportation policies and promoting non-polluting
   modes of transportation, we can contribute to a cleaner and healthier
   urban environment.},
