   BEEUE; Int Clean Energy Talent Program; UNiLAB},
Abstract = {Along with the rapid development of urban economy, the shortage of water
   resources and air pollution are becoming major challenges for
   sustainable urban development. The emission of particulate matter 2.5
   (PM2.5) is strongly associated with industrialization processes, which
   is also intertwined with water utilization processes. Currently, several
   clean air action policies and water conservation policies have been
   issued in China in order to improve the air quality and protect water
   resources, while the connections between these two environmental
   elements are less investigated. In this paper, linkage analysis, which
   descended from input-output analysis, is used to investigate water-PM2.5
   nexus in Beijing. Via analysis of backward linkage and forward linkage,
   the major sectors and pathways associating with water consumption and
   PM2.5 emission are revealed intuitively. We also examined upstream and
   downstream resource flows in the economic network of Beijing, and
   characterized the economic role as well as water consumption and PM2.5
   emission of each sector along the entire supply chain by linkage
   analysis. Copyright (C) 2018 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.},
