   Hong Kong Inst Util Specialists},
Abstract = {For optimizing construction of green ecology landscape water system,
   three basic principles were proposed to design the shore space near
   water, which were ecology, integrity and stable principle respectively.
   These three principles were taken as constraint conditions after they
   were dealed with quantificationally, and quality, progress and
   investment were considered as decision-making variables, at the same
   time, the minimum annual average investment was chosen as objective
   function. A linear programming model for optimizing construction of the
   ecology landscape water system was established and applied to actual
   engineering projects. The use of soil, soil microbes and plants to build
   urban water purification systems, water quality monitoring and
   evaluation through ecological engineering and bio-engineering techniques
   for pollution control effects, simulation analysis of water input costs,
   environmental remediation, development of basic ecological restoration
   technology for urban water environment rehabilitation services, basic
   ecological restoration techniques developed based on the integration and
   improvement to make it suitable for more areas. This paper analyzed the
   economy and technology feasibility of constructed wetland system
   pilot-scale technic engineering economy analysis form of Yangzhou
   Polytechnic University artificial lake also. Results show the present
   model can obtain an excellent balance between social, economic and
   environmental benefits, which is a good guide for construction of the
   ecology landscape water system.},
