   ELECTR NETWORK, SEP 26-OCT 02, 2020},
Organization = {Inst Elect \& Elect Engineers; Inst Elect \& Elect Engineers Geoscience
   \& Remote Sensing Soc},
Abstract = {The ever increasing resolution of synthetic aperture radar (SAR) images
   have made accurate scene understanding possible. However, the rich
   visual context information in SAR images is not yet well explored for
   model construction, which limited the performance of traditional target
   detectors. In this paper, we propose a visual context aware approach to
   mimic the human visual perception mechanism for ship detection from
   high-resolution SAR imagery. Rather than considering target as a group
   of individual scatters, we adopt object-level selective search to
   efficiently locate sparse targets from wide SAR scenes. To verify the
   effectiveness of the proposed method, we test it along with the Hebbian
   neural network approach on several high-resolution SAR images.
   Experimental results show that the proposed approach is quite robust
   under different imaging conditions and can correctly detect ship targets
   in a rapid manner.},
