   System, at the 1998 Western MultiConference, SAN DIEGO, CA, JAN 11-14,
   1998},
Organization = {Soc Comp Simulat Int; Encyclopedia Life Support Syst},
Abstract = {The aim of this paper is to present a survey over the air pollution
   simulation system DYMOS and its applications for air quality management
   of urban and industrial areas at different sites and in different
   contexts. In order to enable the compilation of a complete and accurate
   picture of the state of the environment or changes to it, integrated
   environmental management decision support systems are needed. For the
   domain air, DYMOS can be used as a basic module of such a management
   decision support system. An air quality management system based on DYMOS
   will permit an integrated quantitative and qualitative analysis of the
   air quality in urban and industrial areas, for historical
   investigations, prediction of trends and planning issues.},
