Note = {30th Medical Informatics Europe (MIE) Conference, European Federat Med
   Informat, Geneva, SWITZERLAND, APR, 2020},
Abstract = {With the vast amounts of data that is being generated today, come new
   possibilities of understanding patient mobility. In this study, of urban
   mobility in ten mega cities worldwide, we try to understand the
   relationship between patients' environment and behaviour with regards to
   venues that provide some kind of medical care. We analyze longitudinal
   mobility data set from ten of the world's megacities and investigate
   urban dynamics and travel patterns in terms of interaction with medical
   centers. Our goal is to investigate universal patterns and gain an
   understanding of where people are coming from when they visit such
   venues and where they go afterwards as well how travel patterns progress
   throughout the day.},
