Note = {4th International Conference of Young Scientists (COYOUS 2011), Prague,
   CZECH REPUBLIC, APR 28, 2011},
Organization = {Czech Univ Life Sci Prague, Fac Forestry \& Wood Sci},
Abstract = {The submitted work deals with the stand structure of the High Tatras
   before and after the wind calamity in November 2004. The data have been
   retrieved from the forest inventory in 1996 and 2006. The work also
   includes a brief summary of the proposed harvesting and silvicultural
   measures. In connection with 2004 calamity, there were changes both in
   the structure of the stands and in the approaches to their tending. The
   proportion of tree felling in protected forests increased. In current
   decennium, the prescription 4.5 times higher but importance is laid on
   the structure of the afforested tree species e.g. European larch 950
   hectares as opposed to previous 90 hectares, sycamore maple 350 hectares
   as opposed to 50 hectares. These are tree species which established
   themselves as resistant and may support the stand architecture in the
   event of similar type of calamities.},
