   Korean Soc Indoor Environm; Soc Indoor Environm},
Abstract = {Indoor concentrations of air pollutants are higher than outdoors and
   therefore, people who nowadays spend the largest part of their time
   indoors are expected to be at high risk due to indoor air pollution. The
   concentration of the indoor air pollutants such as formaldehyde,
   ammonia, benzene, NOx and other volatile organic compounds are usually
   not acceptable with respect to human health aspects. In the present
   work, some innovative considerations in modeling formaldehyde
   concentration are considered. The result indicates as to the
   circumstances mentioned below, i.e., air leakage, nature ventilation,
   plants, plants combined with air ventilation, about 20 hours later, the
   formaldehyde concentrations are 208, 5, 178 and 5 mu g/m(3),
   respectively. Natural ventilation has the excellent effect in
   eliminating formaldehyde. Plant also has an effect on the purification,
   but its effect is not as good as natural ventilation.},
