Note = {5th Eurasian Waste Management Symposium (EWMS), Istanbul, TURKEY, OCT
   26-28, 2020},
Organization = {Yildiz Tech Univ, Environm Engn Dept; ISTAC Inc; Int Waste Working Grp;
   T C Cevre Sehircili Bakanligi; Turkish Airlines; Istanbul Convent \&
   Visitors Bur; Cevre Norm; Artemis Aritim; Eced Cevre Danismanlik
   Muhendislik Hizmetleri San Ve Tic Ltd Sti; Ciftligim Gubre; MSB ARGE
   Cevre Enerji Teknolojileri Muh Egitim Dans Ltd Sti; Tin Muhendislik;
   Muhendislik Ar Ge Egitim \& Danismanlik Ltd Sti; Aktan; Galaksi},
Abstract = {Landfill leachate is approximately 55 times more polluted than domestic
   wastewater. Garbage leachate waters, which have harmful effects on the
   environment, end their living life in the environment. Therefore, it
   must be treated.
   Membrane Bioreactor System is the system in which garbage leachate is
   treated most efficiently. If the system uses nanofiltration membranes,
   there will be a problem of concentrated garbage leachate formation.
   Concentrate of Nanofiltration Membranes is a type of wastewater that is
   very difficult to treat. Although there are many purification processes
   in the literature, the application is almost non-existent. In this
   context; chemical precipitation, Membrane Distillation Process
   purification, High Efficiency Reverse Osmosis System, Electrodialysis
   Process and Evaporation systems have been tried.
   Considering the benefit / cost among these systems, the best process was
   the High Efficiency Reverse Osmosis System.},
