   Nicosia, CYPRUS, JUN 12-14, 2006},
Organization = {Chalmers Univ Technol},
Abstract = {The use of commercially available cation exchange cartridges for the
   on/off-line removal of the major interferences of platinum group
   elements (PGEs) during analysis by inductively coupled plasma mass
   spectrometry (ICP-MS) was investigated and the method was validated
   using standard solutions and a certified reference material (BCR-723),
   road dust. The developed method was then applied to the analysis of
   dated sediment cores taken from the Venetian Lagoon. The results
   obtained showed enrichment for the PGEs when compared to the mean
   crustal values, and were in good agreement with the results found by
   other research groups for sediments from different parts of the globe.},
