   07-09, 2017},
Organization = {Malaysian Tech Scientist Assoc},
Abstract = {This paper uses Multi-User Virtual Environment (MUVE) to identify the
   indicators needed by the instructors to improve students' learning
   experience in virtual learning environment. An adapted MUVE indicator of
   Community of Inquiry (COI) is used as the basis of the experiment. The
   adapted MUVE indicators are grouped based on the related categories
   demonstrated in other related research. The result demonstrates that the
   instructors' involvement in a virtual learning environment does provide
   positive learning environment to the students which may also increase
   their learning performance. The adapted MUVE indicators was found to
   provide valuable insights for the instructor to conduct the class in the
   virtual environment.},
