   Hong Kong Inst Util Specialists},
Abstract = {Gentrification has focused on how to boost the incidence of urban
   renaissance by means of immigrating middle class into a decayed built
   environment. Recently, the works of gentrification have been regarded as
   the main engine driver of gentrification, a `public policy' which seeks
   to use positive gentrification as an engine of urban renaissance.
   Followed by the turn of main paradigm of ``third wave{''}
   gentrification, the research of `studentification' implies an emerging
   topic of gentrification. In addition to the same description of a new
   group community in the invasion and succession process of ecological
   community change, the research object has been transformed from
   middle-class communities to student ones. Student groups, seen as a new
   migrant population, and its influence on the original community fabrics,
   including the spatial distribution in communities facing cultural,
   social, environmental conflicts, and land use planning and development
   control to the student housing issue, will become the important contents
   of researching studentification. Therefore, a priori based on the
   outcome of the U K, the paper will use the results of practical
   experience and examine the experience of Taiwan's studentification.
   Taking three village communities surrounding HsinKuo University and
   Leader University in Tainan City as an example, the paper explores
   whether studentification has occurred in Taiwan. Then, it argue that
   studentification indeed affects these communities in terms of social,
   economic, cultural, and physical dimensions.},
