Note = {5th International Workshop on Energy and Environment of Residential
   Buildings/3rd International Conference on Built Environment and Public
   Health, Guilin, PEOPLES R CHINA, MAY 29-31, 2009},
Organization = {Hunan Univ; Univ Hong Kong; Tsinghua Univ},
Abstract = {The aim of this paper is to research the characteristic of natural
   ventilation in the tall residential building with the atrium in stack
   effect. The multizone air-flow and contaminant transport model is
   selected to simulate the diffirent open area of the tall residential
   building with the atrium in stack effect within an urban settings and
   exposed to all erban atmospheric boundary layer. The results from the
   study show that the horizontal airflow takes a breath contribution to
   natural ventilation rate of the tall residential building with the
   atrium when stack effect works. It is also found in this research that
   the top open area plays a decisive role in the ventilation of the atrium
   in stack effect. Usually only one horizontal passage exists for actual
   tall buildings with the atrium, so the case of one horizontal passage is
   studied in this paper. The horizontal passage lies in relatively height
   position of the building which is more favorable to natural ventilation
   of this building when only one horizontal passage is considered in stack
   effect. Achieved results are significant to the design of the tall,
   residential building with the atrium,especially to the nature
   ventilation design of the tall residential building with the atrium.},
