   ALBUQUERQUE, NM, NOV 09-13, 1996},
Organization = {Soc Amer Foresters},
Abstract = {Historically. natural resource management as practiced by the Apache
   people, was based on a philosophy of strict adherence to spiritual ties
   to the land. Activities were controlled by strong reverence for nature's
   bounty and shortage. The result was a mostly benign impact on
   ecosystems. With the Reservation policy came land management
   disenfranchised from the spiritual and cultural, and founded in 20th
   century philosophies of conservation and economic exploitation The
   result has been highly ``unbalanced{''} or unhealthy ecosystems. The
   Apache people at San Carlos are now faced with the prospects of
   restoring these ecosystems to their former, ``balanced{''} state.},
