   (ESE 2016)},
Year = {2016},
Pages = {17-25},
Note = {International Conference on Environmental Science and Engineering (ESE),
   Guilin, PEOPLES R CHINA, APR 15-17, 2016},
Abstract = {Perfluorinated compounds have some good properties, for example,
   chemical stability, high surface activity, thermal stability,
   hydrophobic and oleophobic properties, etc. It also widely used in water
   repellent, anti-oil fields, dust agents, anti-lipid agent, surfactant
   living consumption, industrial production, and so on. But there are also
   persistent, bioaccumulative, refractory and difficult to volatility and
   widespread, serious threat to human health and the environment with
   carcinogenic, teratogenic, and mutagenic threat. The degrading strains
   of perfluorinated compounds from urban sewage and sewage treatment
   sludge degrading were isolated and studies in this study for analyzed
   with the physiological, biochemical, growth characteristics, and the
   strains identified of 16S rDNA. The results showed that two-degrading
   strains have been founded. Degrading strains 1 grown after 20h in the
   medium into the logarithmic growth phase, logarithmic phase of about
   15h; at a pH within the range of normal growth can be 6 similar to 9, pH
   optimum for the growth conditions 7. It was identified as
   Stenotrophomonas maltophilia, and its sequence number in Gene bank was
   GQ287630, and sequence of length was measured as 1462bp. Degrading
   strain 2 grown in the mediums 3h entered the logarithmic growth phase,
   logarithmic phase of about 19h; pH optimum growth conditions for the 7.
   It was identified as Myroides spp., sequence number in Gene bank was
   EU373431, and sequence of length was measured as 1409bp.},
